MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Filter+', content: '**Filter+** A flexible FX box that allows deploying any waveshaper and filter from The Grid directly onto a track. Verwendung: Applying a wide range of filters and waveshapers for sound design and processing. Parameter: Modulation Source: Controls the modulation sources available for the filter and waveshaper. (niedrig=Stereo LFO provides rhythmic modulation., hoch=Audio input allows for dynamic, '});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Fizz', content: '**Fizz** A modern Character filter for spreading harmonic nodes around with a moving formant sensibility, operating inside a stereo, resonant low-pass filter. Verwendung: Use for adding formant-based character and harmonic spreading to audio signals. Kategorie: filter Parameter: Drive: Input saturation (niedrig=clean, hoch=saturated); Cutoff: Filter cutoff frequency (niedrig=fizz in low frequencie'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Flanger', content: '**Flanger** A flanger effect with adjustable LFO and feedback parameters for magnitude and phase. It can be set to retrigger on incoming note messages. Verwendung: Creating classic flanger effects with adjustable feedback and phase controls, ideal for rhythmic modulation. Parameter: Neg.: Controls the phase inversion of the feedback signal. (niedrig=No phase inversion., hoch=Maximum phase inversio'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Flanger+', content: '**Flanger+** A flanger effect with four different Character modes, each with unique DSP architecture. It also includes options for alternate character, stereo inversion, manual override, and added dirt. Verwendung: Creating dynamic and textured flanger effects with various styles, from digital to classic pedal-style. Parameter: Added Dirt: Adds a small amount of noise for additional coloring. (nie'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Floor', content: '**Floor** Rounds all decimal values down to the previous integer Verwendung: Use when you need to round down decimal values for precise signal processing'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Focus', content: '**Focus** A component-model of the renowned Pultec MEQ-5, but with variable Color options and other modern niceties. A good mid-focused EQ with pre-set frequency choices in a sound\'s power regions. Verwendung: For mid-focused EQ with pre-set frequency choices and variable Color options. Parameter: High Boost Amount: Selects the frequency for the high boost filter. (niedrig=Less boost, hoch=More bo'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Follower', content: '**Follower** A symmetric envelope extractor. Verwendung: For extracting symmetric envelope information from an audio signal. Tipps: Use the envelope extractor to control the behavior of other devices.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Follower-RF', content: '**Follower-RF** An envelope extractor with segment times. Verwendung: For extracting envelope information from an audio signal with segment times. Tipps: Use the segment times to control the envelope\'s behavior.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Freq Shift+', content: '**Freq Shift+** Analog-style frequency shifter with feedback, filtering, and phase modulation Verwendung: Metallic shimmering effects, Doppler-like shifts, creating inharmonic timbres Kategorie: fx Parameter: Feedback Low-cut / High-cut: Filters in feedback path (niedrig=filtering more of feedback, hoch=feedback passes through unfiltered); Feedback: Amount of shifted signal fed back (niedrig=singl'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Freq Shifter', content: '**Freq Shifter** A frequency shifter with an adjustable frequency range that can distribute frequency shifts across the stereo field. Verwendung: Shifting the frequency of audio signals for creative sound design or pitch manipulation. Parameter: Frequency Range: Adjusts the range of frequency shifting applied to the audio signal. (niedrig=Minimal frequency shift., hoch=More pronounced frequency sh'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Freq Split', content: '**Freq Split** Divides the signal into adjacent frequency groups and sorts them into one of the four channels for individual mixing and processing. Verwendung: Splitting audio into frequency bands for detailed mixing and processing with different effects on each channel. Parameter: Spectral Limiter Threshold: Caps each individual frequency band at the set threshold. (niedrig=Lower limit for freque'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Freq → Pitch', content: '**Freq → Pitch** Converts Hertz (or kilohertz) to pitch, with optional stereo detune Verwendung: Use to convert frequency values to pitch for modulation or control purposes. Parameter: Detune: Adjusts the stereo detune of the pitch signal. (niedrig=No detune applied., hoch=Maximum stereo detune.). Tipp: Use detune to add width or stereo imaging to the pitch signal.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gain - Vol', content: '**Gain - Vol** Volume gain control Verwendung: Adjusting gain based on volume'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gain - dB', content: '**Gain - dB** Decibel gain control Verwendung: Adjusting gain in decibels'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gate', content: '**Gate** A noise gate with sidechain input and an FX device chain for the control signal. Verwendung: For eliminating unwanted noise between notes. Parameter: FX Device Chain: Allows for additional processing of the control signal. (niedrig=No additional processing applied to the control signal., hoch=Additional FX devices can be used to shape the control signal.). Tipp: Use the FX device chain to'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gate In', content: '**Gate In** A module that receives gate signals and can be used to control voice activation. Verwendung: To trigger and sustain voices based on incoming gate signals. Tipps: Disable Affect Voice Lifetime by default to avoid unintended voice sustain.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gate Length', content: '**Gate Length** Produces a logic pulse of set duration on trigger Verwendung: Use to control the duration of logic pulses for rhythmic or sequencing tasks Parameter: Length: Sets the duration of the logic pulse (niedrig=The logic pulse has a shorter duration, hoch=The logic pulse has a longer duration). Tipp: Use this device to create precise logic pulses'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gate Repeat', content: '**Gate Repeat** Produces repeated logic pulses of set duration while input is high Verwendung: Use to generate continuous logic pulses for looping or rhythmic patterns Parameter: Length: Sets the duration of the repeated logic pulses (niedrig=The repeated logic pulses have a shorter duration, hoch=The repeated logic pulses have a longer duration). Tipp: Use this device to create repeated logic pul'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Gates', content: '**Gates** Event sequencer Verwendung: Used to generate event sequences based on phase signals'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Globals', content: '**Globals** Provides modulator signals for three project-wide controls: Fill, A◆B, and Play. Verwendung: For global control over project parameters like Fill mode, crossfader, and transport state. Tipps: Route hardware controllers or automation to these signals for real-time control of multiple tracks.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Grid', content: '**Grid** A modular system for constructing patches using various Grid types. Verwendung: For creating complex audio effects or note processing chains. Parameter: Modulation Source: A modulation source for the instrument\'s signal, such as amplitude envelope or zone parameters. (niedrig=Minimal modulation effect., hoch=Maximum modulation effect.). Tipp: Use modulation sources to add dynamic movement'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW CV In', content: '**HW CV In** A method for using external control voltage signals for modulation. Verwendung: To modulate parameters based on external control voltage signals. Parameter: AC/DC Mode: Toggles between alternating current (AC) and direct current (DC) modes for the control voltage signal. (niedrig=Signal is in AC mode, which removes the DC offset., hoch=Signal is in DC mode, which includes the DC offse'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW CV Instrument', content: '**HW CV Instrument** Routes incoming note messages as CV signals. It has separate paths for Pitch CV Out and Gate Out triggers. Verwendung: For controlling external hardware synthesizers with Bitwig Studio. Parameter: Latency Offset: Adjusts the latency offset in samples to synchronize the audio signal. (niedrig=No latency offset applied., hoch=A larger latency offset is applied, which can be used'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW CV Out', content: '**HW CV Out** Sends a CV signal out through a set port of your audio interface via a parameter knob. It includes an AC switch and a low-pass filter control. Verwendung: For sending control signals to external hardware modules. Parameter: Low-Pass Filter: Applies a low-pass filter to the outgoing CV signal to add lag or smoothing. (niedrig=Minimal filtering, resulting in a faster response., hoch=Mo'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW Clock Out', content: '**HW Clock Out** Sends CV clock signals through set ports of your audio interface. It has two paths for clock signal output. Verwendung: For synchronizing external hardware with Bitwig Studio\'s tempo. Parameter: Signal Type: Determines the type of clock signal output (e.g., continuous, on play, on stop, per note). (niedrig=Sends a signal only at specific events (e.g., on play or stop)., hoch=Sends'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW FX', content: '**HW FX** Routes incoming stereo audio signals out of the track and system, then returns another stereo signal back. Verwendung: For integrating external effect units into your Bitwig Studio setup. Tipps: Make sure the return signal is properly routed back into the system for processing.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:HW Instrument', content: '**HW Instrument** Routes incoming note signals as MIDI and returns the resultant audio. It includes settings for MIDI output ports and MPE support. Verwendung: For controlling external hardware synthesizers with Bitwig Studio. Tipps: Use the MPE option for expressive control with note expressions.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Hard Clip', content: '**Hard Clip** Simple clipper, with optional Anti-aliasing mode Verwendung: For hard clipping signals with optional aliasing control'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Harmonic Split', content: '**Harmonic Split** Tracks the fundamental of the incoming sound, splitting nonharmonics into one channel and dividing harmonics between two channels. Verwendung: Separating harmonics for individual processing, such as adding distortion or reverb to specific harmonic groups. Parameter: Amplitude Detection Threshold: Sets the amplitude level for detecting fundamental frequencies. (niedrig=Includes m'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Harmonize', content: '**Harmonize** A note transposer that conforms incoming notes based on the active note messages of a different track (Harmony Source). Verwendung: Creating harmonized versions of a melody or chord progression using a different track as a reference. Tipps: Define a Pattern Key to improve the device\'s logic and ensure proper harmonization.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Heat', content: '**Heat** A Character S-shaped clipper that starts soft but can drive hard Verwendung: For soft to hard clipping with a unique curve and aliasing control Kategorie: shaper Parameter: Anti-aliasing: Enables smoothed response of the clipper. (niedrig=No smoothing, potentially introducing aliasing., hoch=Smoothed response, reducing aliasing artifacts.). Tipp: Enable for cleaner, smoother clipping.; Dr'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Hi-hat', content: '**Hi-hat** Drum element instruments that use incoming note signals to synthesize audio. Verwendung: For creating hi-hat sounds using MIDI input. Tipps: Use the XY grid interface for intuitive control of multiple parameters.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:High-pass', content: '**High-pass** High-pass filter with adjustable slope Verwendung: For removing low-frequency content and emphasizing higher frequencies'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Hold', content: '**Hold** Level sustainer Verwendung: Sustaining signal levels'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Howl', content: '**Howl** A Character wave folder that puts different parts of the signal into loud focus Verwendung: For emphasizing different parts of the signal with wave folding Kategorie: shaper Parameter: Anti-aliasing: Enables smoothed response of the wave folder. (niedrig=No smoothing, potentially introducing aliasing., hoch=Smoothed response, reducing aliasing artifacts.). Tipp: Enable for cleaner, smooth'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Humanize', content: '**Humanize** Randomizes aspects of notes such as timing, velocity, and whether notes are played early or late. Verwendung: Adding life to the timing of any input, mutating sequenced passages, and randomizing triggered note clips. Parameter: Velocity: Applies a bipolar amount of randomization to each note\'s velocity. (niedrig=Lower velocity on notes., hoch=Higher velocity on notes.). Tipp: Use Velo'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Instrument Layer', content: '**Instrument Layer** A container that houses multiple instruments in parallel, each with its own internal mixer controls. Verwendung: To layer multiple instruments or sounds simultaneously with independent control over each. Tipps: Use the internal mixer controls to adjust the levels of each instrument chain independently.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Instrument Selector', content: '**Instrument Selector** A container that houses multiple instruments and their associated device chains, allowing only one instrument chain to receive new notes at a time. Verwendung: To switch between different instrument layers based on note input, MIDI controllers, or automation. Parameter: Index: Controls the currently active layer or instrument chain. (niedrig=Selects the first layer or instr'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Invert', content: '**Invert** Reverses the polarity (× -1) of the incoming signal, with Stereo-ness option Verwendung: Use to invert a signal\'s polarity for creative effects or to match signal phase. Parameter: Stereo-ness: Controls the stereo processing of the signal (niedrig=Mono signal processing, hoch=Stereo signal processing). Tipp: Set to 1 for full stereo processing'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Key Filter', content: '**Key Filter** A note transposer that corrects or removes notes that do not match a set key and mode. Notes can also be shifted before transposition. Verwendung: Ensuring notes conform to a specific key or mode, or filtering out dissonant notes. Parameter: Mode: Sets the mode (e.g., major, minor) to which incoming notes should conform. (niedrig=Notes are filtered to match the mode., hoch=Notes are'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Key On', content: '**Key On** Supplies note gate signals from a specified note and channel Verwendung: Triggering notes based on specific MIDI inputs'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Keys Held', content: '**Keys Held** Number of keys currently held Verwendung: Tracking how many keys are being pressed simultaneously'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Keyswitches', content: '**Keyswitches** Designated notes set the target layer (you define the lowest keyswitch; so if set to note C2 and the Selector has 3 layers, C2 switches to layer 1, C#2 switches to layer two, and D2 switches to layer 3). Verwendung: Good for film scoring with different sounds and articulations. Parameter: Lowest Keypress: The lowest keyswitch that triggers the first layer. (niedrig=Sets the lowest '});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Keytrack', content: '**Keytrack** A method for using incoming MIDI and note messages for modulation. Verwendung: To modulate parameters based on incoming MIDI notes. Tipps: Use this device to create modulation effects that respond to MIDI note input.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Keytrack+', content: '**Keytrack+** Uses an embedded Curve Editor for drawing, saving, or loading keytracking curves. Verwendung: To create and apply keytracking curves for modulation based on note pitch. Parameter: Curve: Draws, saves, or loads keytracking curves for modulation based on note pitch. (niedrig=No keytracking modulation., hoch=Full keytracking modulation based on the drawn curve.). Tipp: Use the Curve Edi'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Kick', content: '**Kick** A kick drum element instrument that uses incoming note signals to synthesize audio. It includes a noise generator, FM synthesis, and filtering for shaping the sound. Verwendung: Creating a wide range of kick drum sounds using noise, FM, and filtering. Parameter: Width: Controls the amount of stereo flutter added to each noise burst. (niedrig=Narrower stereo image, more centered sound., ho'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:LFO', content: '**LFO** A fully functional low-frequency oscillator with shape, phase, and polarity controls. Verwendung: Creating complex modulation patterns with various reset modes and polyphonic options. Kategorie: lfo Parameter: Depth: Modulation amount at destination (niedrig=subtle modulation, hoch=wide modulation swing); Waveform: LFO shape: Sine, Triangle, Saw, Square, S/H (niedrig=smooth shapes (Sine/Tr'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:LFO MOD', content: '**LFO MOD** A modulator that provides two low-frequency, tempo-syncable oscillators as independent modulation sources. Verwendung: For creating rhythmic or tempo-synced modulation effects. Tipps: Use in conjunction with filters or effects for dynamic modulation.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:LFO Modulator', content: '**LFO Modulator** A low-frequency oscillator used to modulate parameters such as filter cutoff, pitch, or amplitude, creating dynamic and evolving sounds. Verwendung: To add movement and variation to synth patches, filter sweeps, or rhythmic modulation. Parameter: Per-Voice: Toggles whether the modulator operates in monophonic or polyphonic mode. (niedrig=Monophonic mode (one control signal for al'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:LR Gain', content: '**LR Gain** Independent gain controls for a signal\'s left and right channels Verwendung: Balancing stereo signals'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Label', content: '**Label** Large text widget Verwendung: Displaying information or labels in the interface'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Ladder', content: '**Ladder** A multimode ladder filter with a built-in LFO, envelope, and envelope follower to modulate the filter\'s frequency. Verwendung: Creating classic analog-style filter effects with modulation capabilities. Parameter: Envelope Follower Attack: Controls how quickly the envelope follower responds to changes in the input signal. (niedrig=Slow response, creating a smoother envelope., hoch=Fast r'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Ladder Filter', content: '**Ladder Filter** Moog-style Ladder-Filter. Klassischer analoger Charakter. Kategorie: filter Parameter: Ladder Filter.Drive; Ladder Filter.Resonance; Ladder Filter.Cutoff'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Lag', content: '**Lag** Lag processor Verwendung: Creating lag effects on signals Kategorie: utility Parameter: Fall: Lag time for falling signals (niedrig=instant response on falling edge, hoch=slow glide downward). Tipp: Apply Lag to Pitch In output for portamento on any oscillator; Rise: Lag time for rising signals (niedrig=instant response on rising edge, hoch=slow glide upward)'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Latch', content: '**Latch** A note sustainer that holds the current note until the next one is received, triggers every other note, or triggers based on velocity thresholds. Verwendung: Creating sustained notes, toggling between notes, or sustaining notes based on velocity. Parameter: Velocity Mode: Triggers every other note around a defined velocity threshold. (niedrig=Notes are not selectively triggered., hoch=No'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Level', content: '**Level** Constant set in decibels Verwendung: Setting a fixed level in decibels'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Level Scaler', content: '**Level Scaler** Scales incoming unipolar signal to a defined decibel range Verwendung: Scaling signals to a specific decibel range'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Limiter', content: '**Limiter** Brickwall-Limiter. True-Peak Detection. Kategorie: dynamics Parameter: Limiter.Lookahead; Limiter.Ceiling'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Lin → dB', content: '**Lin → dB** Converts linear amplitudes to decibel values Verwendung: Use to convert linear amplitude values to decibels for audio processing'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Log', content: '**Log** Provides either log2x, logex, or log10x of the incoming signal (x), depending on the Base parameter Verwendung: Use to apply logarithmic scaling to signals for dynamic range control Parameter: Base: Determines the base of the logarithmic function (log2x, logex, or log10x) (niedrig=The logarithmic function uses a lower base, resulting in a slower increase in signal values, hoch=The logarith'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Logic Delay', content: '**Logic Delay** Delays the high- or low-logic states Verwendung: Use to introduce delays in logic signals for timing or sequencing Parameter: Delay: Delays the high- or low-logic states (niedrig=The delay is shorter, resulting in a quicker response, hoch=The delay is longer, resulting in a slower response). Tipp: Use this device to delay logic signals for timing purposes'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Long Delay', content: '**Long Delay** Delay set in time or beat units; also allows feedback connections Verwendung: Creating longer delay effects with feedback Kategorie: fx Parameter: Feedback: How much of the delayed signal feeds back into the delay (niedrig=single repeat, hoch=many decaying repeats). Tipp: High feedback + tempo sync = classic dub delay; Delay Time: Time between original and delayed signal (niedrig=sh'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Loud Split', content: '**Loud Split** Splits incoming sound into three levels: Quiet, Mid, and Loud, allowing individual mixing and processing of each portion. Verwendung: Use for dynamic range control and parallel processing of different signal levels. Parameter: Tilt: Favors high frequencies (positive) or low frequencies (negative) before channel splitting. (niedrig=Favors low frequencies., hoch=Favors high frequencie'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Low-pass', content: '**Low-pass** Low-pass filter with adjustable slope Verwendung: For removing high-frequency content and emphasizing lower frequencies'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Low-pass LD', content: '**Low-pass LD** A resonant low-pass ladder filter. Verwendung: For filtering out high frequencies and shaping the sound with resonance. Kategorie: filter Parameter: Resonance: Ladder resonance / Q (niedrig=no resonant peak, hoch=strong resonant peak, self-oscillation at max). Tipp: Classic Moog style: resonance around 0.6–0.8 for character without self-oscillation; Cutoff: Filter cutoff frequency '});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Low-pass MG', content: '**Low-pass MG** A Moog-inspired low-pass filter with mix buss saturation via the Drive control Verwendung: Adding warmth and saturation to audio signals Kategorie: filter Parameter: Drive: Input saturation level (niedrig=clean, hoch=overdriven, harmonically rich). Tipp: Drive into the filter for warm saturation characteristic of Moog circuits; Resonance: Filter resonance (niedrig=smooth filter, ho'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:MIDI', content: '**MIDI** A module to extract either continuous controller (CC), PRESSURE, or pitch BEND messages arriving at the device\'s input. Verwendung: To extract and process MIDI controller data for modulation. Parameter: Pitch Bend: Controls the pitch bend message to be extracted for modulation. (niedrig=No pitch bend modulation., hoch=Maximum pitch bend modulation.). Tipp: Use Pitch Bend for modulation ba'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:MIDI CC', content: '**MIDI CC** A vehicle for sending any MIDI continuous controller (CC) messages via eight parameter knobs. A global MIDI Channel can be set. Verwendung: Sending MIDI CC messages to control external devices or plugins. Tipps: Set the global MIDI channel to ensure messages are sent to the correct device.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:MIDI Program Change', content: '**MIDI Program Change** A vehicle for sending a MIDI program change message at project load and/or manually via the Send trigger button. It allows sending all or individual components of a two-byte bank select message. Verwendung: Changing presets or programs on MIDI devices or plugins. Parameter: Anti Click: Fades the nested chain\'s output using an adjustable Decay time before sending MIDI messag'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:MIDI Song Select', content: '**MIDI Song Select** A vehicle for sending a MIDI song select message at project load and/or via a manual Send trigger button. Verwendung: Selecting a specific song or sequence on MIDI devices. Tipps: Use this to control song selection on external MIDI hardware or software.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Macro', content: '**Macro** One continuous knob control for modulation. Verwendung: For adjusting modulation parameters in real-time or via automation. Tipps: Use in conjunction with other modulators for dynamic control over sound parameters.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Macro-4', content: '**Macro-4** Four independent, continuous knob controls. Verwendung: Controlling multiple parameters simultaneously with individual knobs.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Math', content: '**Math** One control source derived from two continuous knob controls using mathematical operations. Verwendung: Combining two control sources with multiplication, addition, or subtraction. Parameter: Operation: Controls the mathematical operation applied to the two signals (Multiply, Add, Subtract, Min, Max). (niedrig=Basic operations like multiplication or addition., hoch=More complex operations'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Merge', content: '**Merge** Router with up to eight in ports, passing one or two adjacent incoming signals out at a time Verwendung: Routing multiple input signals to output'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Micro-pitch', content: '**Micro-pitch** Provides micro- and macro-tuning for each note type and octave, with an Amount control to moderate pitch offsets toward standard equal temperament. Verwendung: Tuning individual notes or octaves, or creating microtonal effects. Parameter: Root Note: Defines the root note that remains in tune. (niedrig=Root note is not defined., hoch=Root note is set for tuning reference.). Tipp: Se'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Mid-Side Split', content: '**Mid-Side Split** A container that splits a stereo signal into mid (centered) and side (panned) components, each with an independent chain. Verwendung: To apply different processing to the center and stereo components of a stereo signal. Parameter: Split Frequency: The frequency at which the stereo signal is split into mid and side components. (niedrig=Lower frequency split for mid and side compo'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:MinMax', content: '**MinMax** Provides the current higher and lower values of two signals Verwendung: Use to compare and extract the maximum or minimum values from two signals'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Mix', content: '**Mix** A control source derived from two continuous fader controls. The output signal is determined by the current crossfade position between the two fader values. Verwendung: To blend or crossfade between two modulation signals. Parameter: Crossfade Position: Controls the balance between the two fader values. (niedrig=More emphasis on the first fader., hoch=More emphasis on the second fader.). T'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Mixer', content: '**Mixer** Stereo mixer for up to six channels Verwendung: Mixing multiple stereo channels'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Mod Delay', content: '**Mod Delay** Modulator delay with internal feedback loop Verwendung: Adding modulated delay effects with feedback Kategorie: fx Parameter: Mix: Wet/dry blend (niedrig=mostly dry signal, hoch=mostly modulated delay); Modulation Depth: Depth of delay time modulation (niedrig=subtle modulation, hoch=strong pitch wobble / flanger sweep). Tipp: Short delay + deep modulation = flanger; longer delay + m'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Modulator Out', content: '**Modulator Out** Makes incoming signals available as a modulator signal Verwendung: Routing signals for modulation purposes'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Multi-note', content: '**Multi-note** A chord builder that allows up to eight notes to play for each received note message, with options for velocity spread, chance, and live note updating. Verwendung: Creating chords from single notes, randomizing velocities, and dynamically updating chords in real time. Parameter: Chance: Sets the likelihood that each note unit will trigger. (niedrig=Low probability of triggering indi'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Multiband Compressor', content: '**Multiband Compressor** A device that allows for independent compression of different frequency bands, with options for tonal coloring and sidechain input. Verwendung: To shape the dynamics of individual frequency ranges in a mix, such as taming harsh frequencies or adding warmth. Parameter: Stereo Independence: Controls the amount of separation between the stereo channels for each analysis band.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Multiband FX-2', content: '**Multiband FX-2** A container that splits incoming audio at a definable frequency, providing independent chains for the audio below and above that frequency. Verwendung: To apply different effects to different frequency ranges of an audio signal. Parameter: Split Frequency: The frequency at which the audio signal is split into two frequency ranges. (niedrig=Lower frequency split for audio process'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Multiband FX-3', content: '**Multiband FX-3** A container that splits incoming audio at two definable frequencies, providing independent chains for the audio below the first frequency, between the two frequencies, and above the second frequency. Verwendung: To apply different effects to three distinct frequency ranges of an audio signal. Parameter: Split Frequency 2: The second frequency at which the audio signal is split i'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:Multiply', content: '**Multiply** Multiplies two signals together Verwendung: Use to modulate signals with multiplication for amplitude or frequency control.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:N-Latch', content: '**N-Latch** Allows trigger signals to alternate between multiple output states Verwendung: Use to manage multiple output states with trigger signals for complex control'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:NAND', content: '**NAND** A logic gate that outputs true if any inputs are false. Verwendung: Used for creating conditional processing that requires at least one condition to be false. Tipps: Can be used to trigger events when any of the signals are inactive.'});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'Device:NOR', content: '**NOR** A logic gate that outputs true if all inputs are false. Verwendung: Used for creating conditional processing that requires all conditions to be false. Tipps: Can be used to trigger events when all signals are inactive.'});
