MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Bitwig Studio 5\'s Live Performance Features#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Bitwig Studio 5\'s Live Performance Features** This is Thavius Beck. Right now I\'d like to talk to you about a brand new feature in Bitwig Studio 5 that really allows you to do much more with clip launching, and this is extremely useful and fun when it comes to live performance. I\'ve done a lot of performances using a clip launcher and a controller that lets me launch clips. Righ', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lniO-QQCdI8', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Bitwig Studio 5\'s Live Performance Features#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Bitwig Studio 5\'s Live Performance Features** have my main behavior, which right now, each clip will launch every bar each clip will start at the beginning, and when I let go, it\'ll just keep doing what it\'s doing. But I have an alternate action over here as well, and I can toggle between this using MIDI. On my Launchpad Pro I can just hold shift. For my alternate action, the qu', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lniO-QQCdI8', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Bitwig\'s Transient Split in action#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Bitwig\'s Transient Split in action** What I might want to do here is Take the transients And maybe... Enhance Their plinky-plucky character a little bit Let\'s go ahead... Okay, maybe bit reduction\'s not the right thing. But a little jitter on the clock and a little chance... Gives a little bit of a splatter to each of those moments That\'s interesting That\'s kinda nice... And the', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B2KTggsWFUg', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2** Hi, Pat Cupo here for Bitwig and I\'d like to introduce you to three brand new, great sounding audio FX as part of the 4.2 update to Bitwig Studio. And they are Chorus+, Flanger+, and Phaser+. I\'ll give you an overview of each device, demo them one by one, then I\'ll combine them in The Grid with the module versions', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z-NYSG1JW7g', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2** pretty much the same setup as Chorus+ with a few main differences. Click through the characters which are DP, MX, TFX, and WA and notice that all four parameters stay the same. So you\'ll always have color and feedback as the X and Y parameters With the LFO speed and depth parameters down below. On the bottom right', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z-NYSG1JW7g', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2#2', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Chorus+ / Flanger+ / Phaser+: New Audio FX in Bitwig Studio 4.2** It lives somewhere between the richness of Chorus+ and the filtered swooshing sound of Flanger+. And as an added bonus There are The Grid module versions of all three Plus FX. Now, when you\'re looking for these FX you can find them under the newly named category Delay FX. These are the same FX you heard earlier Th', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z-NYSG1JW7g', chunk_index: 2});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Clip Aliases – New in Bitwig Studio 6#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Clip Aliases – New in Bitwig Studio 6** Music is based on structure and form. Some patterns loop immediately and others come back later. Clip aliases let you share content or patterns between different clips on the same track. This can work for note clips, audio clips, or automation clips. Creating an alias clip is as simple as dragging with a different modifier. Once multiple c', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tjzqDdJT0q0', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Comping in Bitwig Studio 4#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Comping in Bitwig Studio 4** Hello everyone, welcome. My name is Pat Cupo, thank you for watching. It is my absolute honor today to introduce to you the brand new comping feature in Bitwig Studio. I\'m a musician, I\'m a producer, and much like probably many of you, I\'ve been really, really hoping for this feature. It\'s finally here. Let\'s check it out. I\'m going to show you the t', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DANWf9gG8Vg', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Comping in Bitwig Studio 4#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Comping in Bitwig Studio 4** right on the spot. I love that each take is automatically given its own color so everything is super clear. All I need to do now is drag over the takes to select take regions until I have a composite that I\'m happy with. Hey, I\'m happy with that. Let\'s drag this clip over to the Arranger. Now, for those looking for some more compositing options, ther', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DANWf9gG8Vg', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Comping in Bitwig Studio 4#2', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Comping in Bitwig Studio 4** on my Mac, I can take the chords from Take one, where I think I had better timing. And the third thing you should know about comping here in Bitwig is the new "Fold To Takes" feature. Let\'s add another percussion part, but this time we\'ll take a longer clip and fold it onto itself. I found this tabla clip that I really like, and I want to make a 2 me', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DANWf9gG8Vg', chunk_index: 2});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Convolution device – New in Bitwig Studio 4.3#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Convolution device – New in Bitwig Studio 4.3** Convolution technology is like a very special filter Running each moment of incoming audio through an entire impulse This is particularly good for obtaining high quality reverbs At a variety that only sampling can provide Bitwig\'s new Convolution device puts this concept into a smart, compact, design The factory content provides hu', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q3-aAkKzTAM', chunk_index: 0});
