MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:How to use Bitwig Studio 5\'s new browsers — 6 tips#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: How to use Bitwig Studio 5\'s new browsers — 6 tips** Bitwig\'s browsers are designed to give you the right options at the right moment That goes for the ever-present browser panel on the right-hand side of the program, as well as the pop-up browser, which you can summon with the numerous + buttons you\'ll find throughout Bitwig Studio. Learning a bit about how the browsers work wi', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ba2lEg1_wIg', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:How to use Bitwig Studio 5\'s new browsers — 6 tips#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: How to use Bitwig Studio 5\'s new browsers — 6 tips** Settings and choose "Use current selections for this context." You can organize your library by creating collections. Right-clicking on any result adds it to your Favorites or your other collections, and the number shows the shortcut for that collection. Find an interesting sound, preset or impulse? Just press the keyboard and', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ba2lEg1_wIg', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Integrating Hardware with Bitwig Studio 101#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Integrating Hardware with Bitwig Studio 101** Bitwig Studio makes it fun and easy to integrate your external hardware, from synths and FX to modular gear, and build a powerful and flexible hybrid setup that combines the best of the worlds of hardware and software. The HW Instrument device lets you play and control external synths with ease. Note FX and modulators add powerful fe', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NxT6blFC2j4', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio** Hi. With Bitwig Studio\'s CV devices, you can easily send control voltage gate and clock signals to and from your Eurorack modules and other CV enabled hardware. In this video, I will show you how to incorporate your CV Gear with Bitwig Studio and add a wide range of functionality to your modular setup. I will mostly focus on Eu', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a-bMcWPDIPM', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio** Coast to audio input 1 of my audio interface and set audio into Channel 1. Now when I press a note, the HW CV instrument device sends gate and pitch to No Coast and receives the audio back, all in one device To automatically tune the oscillator, press Tune, which will then play notes from low to high and calibrate the oscillato', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a-bMcWPDIPM', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio#2', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio** the output channel accordingly. Now when you press play, the module runs in sync with Bitwig The HW Clock Out device can be adjusted for many different scenarios and needs. You can choose between different sync modes from the dropdown menu at the top. You can switch from a clock to a gate signal, in case your module requires it', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a-bMcWPDIPM', chunk_index: 2});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio#3', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Integrating Your Modular Setup with Bitwig Studio** device and assign it to another channel Add as many CV Out devices as your interface supports and combine them with modulators to create unique, complex patches that you can save as presets for other projects CV from your modules can also be used to control devices in Bitwig Studio. To control a parameter from an external CV so', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a-bMcWPDIPM', chunk_index: 3});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Introducing Note Grid [Bitwig Studio 4.2]#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Introducing Note Grid [Bitwig Studio 4.2]** The Grid is Bitwig Studio\'s modular sound design environment Where building instruments and audio effects is beautiful and fun. In Bitwig 4.2, a third device is joining Poly Grid and FX Grid: Note Grid. Note Grid is made to process notes or even generate them With access to The Grid\'s 184 modules and polyphonic structure. To kick thing', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXxhREOyPI8', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Introducing Note Grid [Bitwig Studio 4.2]#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Introducing Note Grid [Bitwig Studio 4.2]** welcome, they\'re family. The Grid is also ready to create notes now all from the Note Out module. The first out port wants a gate signal and with each pulse it receives a note is born. Pitch velocity and channel can be set directly. And since sequencer patches tend to be mono It\'s often helpful to have multiple Note Out modules. Groove', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXxhREOyPI8', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Key Signature – New in Bitwig Studio 6#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Key Signature – New in Bitwig Studio 6** A song\'s key is its musical coloring lines. Key signature in Bitwig Studio can both guide your work and animate your note FX. Key signature lives beside tempo and other global settings in the transport. It comprises two parameters. Root Key defines the anchor pitch. All Piano Roll Editors will highlight this note. And Scale represents the', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5YYoVofg0c8', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs** Hey everyone, I\'m Pat Cupo, and I\'d like to introduce you to Sculpt, Focus and Tilt, three brand-new EQs in Bitwig Studio 5.2. This trio of EQs is inspired by classic hardware and brings a natural musicality to the task of shaping sound. Sculpt inherited the controls and components of the renowned Pultec EQP-1, a broadband hardwa', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pV8ePzXaNGo', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs** three goals. First, I need to tame the noisy pickups on my bass, and I\'ll use the high cut for that. Then, I didn\'t use my active pickups, and there\'s no big bass boost coming from my guitar, so I\'ll use the bass boost and cut to dial in the low end. Lastly, I want to emphasize the picked strings a bit. I\'ll use the peak boost an', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pV8ePzXaNGo', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs#2', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Learn Bitwig Studio 5.2\'s Hardware-Inspired EQs** a gradual ramp towards an S-curve. And once again, there\'s a helpful visual display with the same color-coding Bitwig users are used to, and the stereoize feature, which you\'ll see next. So the concept of Tilt EQ is pretty self-explanatory, but what isn\'t straightforward is when you might want to use one. You could try using tilt', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pV8ePzXaNGo', chunk_index: 2});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Learn Stepwise, Bitwig\'s Step Sequencing Device#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Learn Stepwise, Bitwig\'s Step Sequencing Device** New in Bitwig Studio 5.3 is Stepwise, a deceptively simple pattern sequencer. Just like music programming, Stepwise starts with adding a few notes This lane\'s velocity is set just on the right If we hold ALT, accented notes are added. Their level is set relatively, so controlling the lane\'s velocity will adjust both normal notes ', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VpmA_Bb3CH8', chunk_index: 0});
