MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]** Hello, and welcome back to Bitwig, featuring The Grid. If I go ahead and grab our basic Poly Grid patch here. I get sound right out of the box. As I play notes, they\'re being articulated. The triangle wave oscillator is being shaped by an amplifier, which is under the control of an attack-release envelope. I\'ve got', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iduRb3wguak', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]** try wiring them into our patch. The easiest way to hear a control signal is to wire it into pitch, because that\'s what our ear is most sensitive to. I\'m going to go ahead and take the output of this AD envelope and put it to the pitch input. Hence the orange port, and the label down below of the triangle wave. At f', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iduRb3wguak', chunk_index: 1});
