MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]#4', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Modular Concepts: Basic Modulations [Bitwig Studio | The Grid]** longer we\'d hear the vibrato. A little bit. But, it\'s still wrong. This isn\'t the envelope we want. If I go back to our Envelope category. Maybe an AR, just like what was in our patch already for amplitude. And now we should have sustain. I\'m going to slow down the fade in time. Maybe a little more. And maybe even ', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iduRb3wguak', chunk_index: 4});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:Modular Concepts: Feedback [Bitwig Studio]#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: Modular Concepts: Feedback [Bitwig Studio]** Welcome back to Bitwig, featuring The Grid. Today\'s modular concept is feedback. The first time most people encountered feedback it was unpleasant, because it was unwanted. But when feedback is created intentionally, like this clearly leftward moving patch cord. You actually have an opportunity to do something colorful and interesting', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bSg0d6UcTE', chunk_index: 0});
