MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:New Note FX in Bitwig Studio 4.1#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: New Note FX in Bitwig Studio 4.1** Bitwig Studio 4.1 is here, and notes are in bloom. There are now 21 note processors in Bitwig, each providing a unique predictable way to treat your note signals. Let\'s take a quick look at the eight new devices, seeking both functional and creative uses. Note Repeats provides countless ways to make notes re-trigger. Timing and everything else ', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2oP92pTmmOM', chunk_index: 0});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:New Note FX in Bitwig Studio 4.1#1', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: New Note FX in Bitwig Studio 4.1** then sends one or more out at a time, this can add a plucky feel to any track. Or, think of strum as a one-shot arpeggiator, spitting out each stack of notes on demand. Bend gives each note a simple pitch envelope. This can be used for glides or glissandos... Or, use a quick bend to design new sounds with any instrument. Finally, Ricochet uses ', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2oP92pTmmOM', chunk_index: 1});
MERGE (d:Document {source: 'YouTube:On Microtuning [Bitwig Studio | Micro-Pitch Device]#0', content: '**Bitwig Tutorial: On Microtuning [Bitwig Studio | Micro-Pitch Device]** Hello, and welcome back to Bitwig. Today we\'re looking at the Micro-pitch device and particularly its presets, including some new additions. We\'re going to take a look at the different categories that the presets include. We\'re gonna look at some of the presets that reshape the keyboard to create something new and a few new p', doc_type: 'youtube_transcript', video_url: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Sm573jmEQs', chunk_index: 0});
